**Definition 6.1 (disjoint request grammar).** Preserve outer frames
`tag U(d) payload` and all original source tags 000–100, Cover 101 and
Next/Select 110. Under tag 111 accept either old Call payload $U(p)$ or

$$
01\,s\,U(r)\,dd,
\qquad s\in\{0,1\},\quad dd\in\{00,01,10,11\}.
\tag{PVC.7}
$$

For $s=0$, $r$ is an acquired package number selecting its latest completed
Call image. For $s=1$, $r$ is a completed view number. $dd$ is the
requested destination. The Convert payload length is $r+6$; a nonempty
unary Call payload beginning 0 consists of that single 0, whereas PVC.7
begins 01. Thus exact exhaustive parsing cannot confuse them. Destination
bits are fixed-width two-bit words, not wire naturals.

Every bit uses RCA Definition 13.2's actual port-38 reader with latch 6
retained until WR and tests in latch 5. Installed Ready first executes
the client-to-handler TOK and reserve CTL. Ingress measures Base, writes
the frame/F, seals, constructs measured length $U(2d+4)$ on a distinct
scratch, full descriptor and native import. No register receives a
mathematical body without these rows. Unknown complete identifiers produce
NoImage or NoView; unsupported layout/version produces UnsupportedVersion.
Other complete noncanonical service payloads use the paid
MalformedServiceFrame arm. Malformed source payloads keep RCA's separate
InvalidSourceFrame exit; they never become service or source success.

